  <running_head>Admonitio.</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" type="heading" level="1" para="true">Admonitio.</l>
    <l n="2" para="true">Profecto si (quod luculenter</l>
    <l n="3">probavi,) authoritate Ecclesiae</l>
    <l n="4">Romanae intelligenda est solius</l>
    <l n="5">Papae authoritas, &amp; nomine Ec-</l>
    <l n="6">clesiae Romanae intelligendum</l>
    <l n="7">est Papale imperium in Reges</l>
    <l n="8">&amp; nationes, robore, pompâ,</l>
    <l n="9">&amp; divitiis illustre: tum si non ult-</l>
    <l n="10">erius ab his &amp; illis suspicitur</l>
    <l n="11">&amp; çolitur illud imperium, quam</l>
    <l n="12">quatenus obductum &amp; fucatum</l>
    <l n="13">est vocabulis, Ecclesiae, Pote-</l>
    <l n="14">statis &amp; Monarchiae Ecclesiasticae</l>
    <l n="15">&amp; spiritualis: si denique quod volunt</l>
    <l n="16">doctores Romanenses, non ulterius Scriptura habet</l>
    <l n="17">authoritatem quam quat-</l>
    <l n="18">enus à Papa probatur:</l>
    <l n="19">tam necessaria consecutione sequetur</l>
    <l n="20">Reges &amp; populos exolutos illa</l>
    <l n="21">fraude vocabulorum quibus Pa-</l>
    <l n="22">pa suum imperium fucat &amp; pro-</l>
    <l n="23">bat, statim id imperii eversuros,</l>
    <l n="24">&amp; con-</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Page is a single column of text; the last line "&amp; con-" is a catchword-style hyphenated continuation at the foot of the column, not a separate catchword. Some ink spots and scan marks are ignored. Watermark "Digitized by Google" ignored.</notes>
</page>
